fix: a slow JOIN drags you out of the buffer you moved to

`switchToChannel` is recorded when the join is requested and acted on when the
server's JOIN arrives, with no timeout and no cancellation — so a slow join, or an
autojoin on reconnect, can pull you away from wherever you went in the meantime.

Clearing it in `switchBuffer` covers every manual switch (list, keyboard, switcher) in
one place, and the intended jump still works: the JOIN handler tests the field before
using it.

